WP24 (2026-11-03) removed the leaderboard evaluator this NOTICE used to cover: the
FlashInfer-Bench and SOL-ExecBench input generators, correctness protocols and timing
protocols in the old eval/leaderboard.py template. What remains of adapted third-party
code, file by file:

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOL-ExecBench
https://github.com/NVIDIA/SOL-ExecBench (commit a9fa080)

  src/forgekernel/card_template/eval/benchkit.py
      the random-input draw and the input name heuristics (_rand_tensor,
      _cast_to_fp4x2, _heuristic_tensor and the _is_* name predicates), adapted from
      src/sol_execbench/core/bench/io.py; they serve the precision record's stress
      draws and the recon tools' probe inputs on a normal task.
  src/forgekernel/binref.py, src/forgekernel/binref_tool.py
      the compiled-solution build conventions (compile_options semantics, top-level
      C/C++/CUDA sources, the CUTLASS include path), following the solution format of
      src/sol_execbench/core/data/solution.py and driver/templates/eval_driver.py.
  src/forgekernel/loop/analytic_floor.py
      the expression grammar of the shapes resolver, following
      src/sol_execbench/core/data/shapes.py.

